1. Monolithic
Monolithic means an application is built as one single, tightly connected unit.
- All functionalities are part of one application.
- Frontend, backend, business logic, and database interactions are generally managed within one system.
- If you make a change in one module, you may need to rebuild and redeploy the entire application.
- Modules are often tightly coupled.

FAST API : fast api is a python framework which is used to build api
